{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"bbc43356-430e-40a9-a14e-41404b640377","agentId":"afed32e1361f5dde3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes. Token-efficient: read only what you need, 1 search per fact, 5 checks, report under 100 words. Do not edit cuore/web/* or cuore/app.py. Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe; patterns: mes-log-mcp/mes/code_feel.py (sourced tables), mes/workup.py (history per code with sessions/timestamps), mes/known_good.py (channel bands), mes/parts.py, mes/experience.py, mes/maintenance_specs.py. Car: 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T.\n\nGoal: make vehicle SYSTEMS a correlational dimension for every technical issue.\n1. mes-log-mcp/mes/systems.py: SYSTEMS (ordered): electrical_supply (battery, alternator, grounds, fuses/BCM feeds), network (CAN buses, gateways), ignition, fuel, evap, air_intake_boost (intake, MAP, turbo, intercooler, hoses), cooling, lubrication (oil), exhaust_emissions, transmission_driveline, brakes_abs, steering, suspension, body_comfort, adas_sensors, hvac. Each {label, components: [...], live_channels: [ids from cuore/live/channels.py that exist], maintenance_items: [maintenance_specs keys], parts: [parts.py keys], depends_on: [{system, why, confidence, source}] (e.g. evap depends on electrical_supply (ESIM/purge valve supply) and fuel (tank, cap, pressure); network depends on electrical_supply (grounds, F82/BCM feeds per the TSBs already in mes/knowledge.py); ignition on electrical_supply; air_intake_boost on exhaust (turbo) etc.: cite sources; UNKNOWN where unsourced). CODE_RULES mapping a code to systems: exact-code table first (P0440/P0455/P0456/P0441/P0457/P1CEA -> evap; P0300-04 -> ignition+fuel; P0171/72 -> fuel+air_intake_boost; U-codes -> network (+electrical_supply as upstream); B1040/U1700 BCM comms -> network; B1176 -> body_comfort; C141B/C141C -> adas_sensors; C104B -> brakes_abs; P0098/P00F5/P105E/P1189 -> air_intake_boost; P1xxx by description keywords), then SAE range fallback (P01xx fuel/air, P03xx ignition/misfire, P04xx emissions/evap, P05xx idle/speed/electrical, P06xx ecm, P07xx-P09xx transmission, C brakes/chassis, B body, U network). systems_for_code(code, description=\"\") -> [{system, role: \"primary\"|\"upstream\", confidence, source}].\n2. correlate(vin) -> {\"by_system\": [{system, codes: [...], sessions: n, first, last, status: active|cleared_unverified|stale|clean}], \"co_occurrence\": [{a, b, sessions_together: n, sessions_a, sessions_b, lift: float, reading: plain sentence}] for system pairs that co-occur in >=2 sessions, \"chains\": [{\"issue\": \"EVAP codes\", \"possible_upstream\": [{system, why, evidence: str|None}]}] built from depends_on, with evidence from the corpus (e.g. network codes present in the same sessions as EVAP codes -> mention; battery voltage readings below known_good band in those sessions if available), \"findings\": [plain sentences, dated]}. Use mes.workup.build(vin) history + session timestamps; simulation excluded. Never present a dependency as proven: use \"could be upstream\" wording with the confidence.\n3. MCP tools in mes-log-mcp/server.py: systems_for_code(code), system_correlation(vin). Expose through a new cuore/services/systems_bridge.py (systems(), systems_for_code, correlate) and cuore/api/systems.py router (GET /systems, /systems/for-code/{code}, /vehicles/{vin}/systems) ; report the include line.\n4. Tests mes-log-mcp/tests/check_systems.py + cuore/tests/check_systems_api.py (5 total): every depends_on has a source or UNKNOWN; P0455 -> evap primary with electrical_supply upstream; U1713 -> network; correlate(real VIN) returns evap and network with sessions >= 4 and at least one co-occurrence row; API 200. Run them + check_server.py."},"uuid":"ed032153-6967-4a28-8581-b858556c83af","timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:41:44.313Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
