{"parentUuid":"e8b2c8a4-b85e-4801-a07e-aed355b06f8e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"afed32e1361f5dde3","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfozyYQciauEHDrHPkRTA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012KQJJz1Kc2pATcu9Cfx6bY","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\parts_bridge.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4986,"cache_read_input_tokens":90601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4986,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012KQJJz1Kc2pATcu9Cfx6bY":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\parts_bridge.py"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a263e4c0-bd14-4cf0-a61a-d8d7b6397368","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfozyYAjpdStydjoYkY33","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"fbb765e7-cae8-44e9-8a47-bf86e2ef8508","timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:43:05.655Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"fbb765e7-cae8-44e9-8a47-bf86e2ef8508","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8b9c6287-d7e2-4fd6-8dbd-dc6c5dce5337","agentId":"afed32e1361f5dde3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012KQJJz1Kc2pATcu9Cfx6bY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"The only module in CUORE that imports :mod:`mes.parts`.\n2\t\n3\t``mes-log-mcp/mes/parts.py`` is being written in parallel by another agent\n4\tand may not exist yet. Every call into it is wrapped and falls back to a\n5\tbuilt-in fixture (shaped exactly like that module's documented contract --\n6\tsee ``_FIXTURE`` below) so the parts page, the ``/api/parts*`` endpoints and\n7\tthe part cards embedded in ``code.html``/``maintenance.html``/\n8\t``oil_change.html``/``brakes_tires.html`` are developable and testable\n9\tbefore it lands. Once ``mes.parts`` exists, nothing here needs to change --\n10\tthe lazy import just starts succeeding and the fixture stops being reached.\n11\t\n12\tContract (``mes.parts``, once it lands): ``get(key)``, ``for_code(code)``,\n13\t``for_job(job)``, ``all()``, each returning / each row shaped::\n14\t\n15\t    {key, name, what_it_does,\n16\t     oem: [{number, brand, note, confidence, source}],\n17\t     supersedes, aftermarket: [{brand, number, confidence, source}],\n18\t     fits, location, related_codes, related_jobs, torque_keys,\n19\t     price: {low, high, currency, as_of, source} | None,\n20\t     buy: [{label, url}],\n21\t     images: [{url, source_page, source_name, kind, licence_note, verified_at}],\n22\t     notes}\n23\t\n24\t``torque_keys`` is a list of keys into the torque libraries -- resolved\n25\there, not by ``mes.parts`` itself, against ``mes.service_specs`` and\n26\t``mes.drivetrain_specs`` (the same two libraries\n27\t``cuore.services.service_bridge`` already reaches through its own bridge),\n28\tso a part card can show \"25 Nm, SINGLE-SOURCE\" without ``mes.parts`` needing\n29\tto duplicate the torque library. A key neither library recognises resolves\n30\tto an UNKNOWN row rather than being dropped, so the card can say so.\n31\t\n32\tEvery public function here degrades to an empty result (\"No part data yet\")\n33\trather than raising -- the one exception is :func:`part`, which returns\n34\t``None`` for an unknown key so the API layer can turn that into a 404.\n35\t\"\"\"\n36\t\n37\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n38\t\n39\tfrom typing import Any, Optional\n40\t\n41\tfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\n42\t\n43\t\n44\t# --- lazy imports, each independently guarded ------------------------------\n45\t\n46\tdef _parts_mod():\n47\t    \"\"\"``mes.parts``, or ``None`` if it has not landed yet.\"\"\"\n48\t    try:\n49\t        from mes import parts as parts_mod\n50\t        return parts_mod\n51\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- must never be why a page 500s\n52\t        return None\n53\t\n54\t\n55\tdef _service_specs():\n56\t    try:\n57\t        from mes import service_specs\n58\t        return service_specs\n59\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n60\t        return None\n61\t\n62\t\n63\tdef _drivetrain_specs():\n64\t    try:\n65\t        from mes import drivetrain_specs\n66\t        return drivetrain_specs\n67\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n68\t        return None\n69\t\n70\t\n71\tdef _model_for_vin(vin: Optional[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n72\t    \"\"\"Best-effort model name for ``vin`` via ``mes.platform``, or ``None``\n73\t    on any failure or an unrecognised VIN -- never raises.\"\"\"\n74\t    if not vin:\n75\t        return None\n76\t    try:\n77\t        from mes import platform as platform_mod\n78\t        model = platform_mod.model_for_vin(vin)\n79\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n80\t        return None\n81\t    return None if model == \"UNKNOWN\" else model\n82\t\n83\t\n84\t# --- fixture: the exact shape mes.parts.get()/for_code()/for_job()/all()\n85\t# will return, used until that module lands (or for any key it does not yet\n86\t# cover). Keyed to things this corpus already knows about -- the Stelvio's\n87\t# chronic P0455/P0456 EVAP family (see project_stelvio_evap.md) and the jobs\n88\t# oil_change.html/maintenance.html/brakes_tires.html already render -- so a\n89\t# developer working on those pages sees real-looking cards immediately. ----\n90\t\n91\t_FIXTURE: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {\n92\t    \"esim\": {\n93\t        \"key\": \"esim\",\n94\t        \"name\": \"EVAP Service/Integrity Monitor (ESIM)\",\n95\t        \"what_it_does\": \"Pressurizes the fuel-vapor system and watches the \"\n96\t                        \"decay rate to detect small and large EVAP leaks. A \"\n97\t                        \"failed self-test or a failed component sets \"\n98\t                        \"P0455/P0456/P0457, not necessarily a leak itself.\",\n99\t        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68245527AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\",\n100\t                 \"note\": \"ESIM / natural-vacuum leak-detection pump assembly\",\n101\t                 \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\",\n102\t                 \"source\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/evap-esim-replacement.21004/\"}],\n103\t        \"supersedes\": [],\n104\t        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Standard Motor Products\", \"number\": \"EVAP1234\",\n105\t                         \"confidence\": \"UNKNOWN\", \"source\": None}],\n106\t        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T (2017-2022)\",\n107\t        \"location\": \"Rear of the fuel tank, inline on the vapor line, ahead of the canister.\",\n108\t        \"related_codes\": [\"P0455\", \"P0456\", \"P0457\"],\n109\t        \"related_jobs\": [\"evap_leak\"],\n110\t        \"torque_keys\": [\"evap_esim_mount\"],\n111\t        \"price\": {\"low\": 180.0, \"high\": 260.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n112\t                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n113\t        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"},\n114\t                {\"label\": \"Mopar eStore\", \"url\": \"https://www.moparonlineparts.com\"}],\n115\t        \"images\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/data/esim-photo.jpg\",\n116\t                    \"source_page\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/evap-esim-replacement.21004/\",\n117\t                    \"source_name\": \"stelvioforum.com\", \"kind\": \"product_photo\",\n118\t                    \"licence_note\": \"forum upload, fair-use reference only\",\n119\t                    \"verified_at\": \"2026-09-20\"}],\n120\t        \"notes\": \"Verified against TSB 18-030-17 before replacing -- that TSB's ECM \"\n121\t                 \"calibration read fixes a false P0456 on some build dates without \"\n122\t                 \"any part being replaced.\",\n123\t    },\n124\t    \"purge_valve\": {\n125\t        \"key\": \"purge_valve\",\n126\t        \"name\": \"EVAP Purge Solenoid Valve\",\n127\t        \"what_it_does\": \"Opens under ECM control to let engine vacuum draw stored fuel \"\n128\t                        \"vapor from the canister into the intake. Stuck closed or \"\n129\t                        \"leaking, it can contribute to a P0455/P0456 decay-rate failure.\",\n130\t        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68093419AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\",\n131\t                 \"note\": \"Purge valve/solenoid\", \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\",\n132\t                 \"source\": \"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/purge-valve-location.9821/\"}],\n133\t        \"supersedes\": [\"68093419A (earlier casting, same fit)\"],\n134\t        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Four Seasons\", \"number\": \"PV1029\",\n135\t                         \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\", \"source\": None}],\n136\t        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T (2017-2022)\",\n137\t        \"location\": \"Intake manifold, driver's side, short hose run to the charcoal canister.\",\n138\t        \"related_codes\": [\"P0455\", \"P0456\"],\n139\t        \"related_jobs\": [\"evap_leak\"],\n140\t        \"torque_keys\": [\"evap_purge_valve_mount\"],\n141\t        \"price\": {\"low\": 45.0, \"high\": 90.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n142\t                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n143\t        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"}],\n144\t        \"images\": [],\n145\t        \"notes\": \"\",\n146\t    },\n147\t    \"oil_filter\": {\n148\t        \"key\": \"oil_filter\",\n149\t        \"name\": \"Engine Oil Filter (cartridge element)\",\n150\t        \"what_it_does\": \"Traps combustion byproducts and wear metal out of circulating oil.\",\n151\t        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68105175AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"cartridge element + housing cap\",\n152\t                 \"confidence\": \"CONFIRMED\",\n153\t                 \"source\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/oil-change-maintenance-reset.19336/\"}],\n154\t        \"supersedes\": [],\n155\t        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Mopar/Mann filter element\", \"number\": \"HU 711/51x\",\n156\t                         \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\", \"source\": None}],\n157\t        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T MultiAir (2017-2022)\",\n158\t        \"location\": \"Top of the engine, cartridge-style housing with a plastic cap.\",\n159\t        \"related_codes\": [],\n160\t        \"related_jobs\": [\"oil_change\"],\n161\t        \"torque_keys\": [\"filter_cap\"],\n162\t        \"price\": {\"low\": 18.0, \"high\": 32.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n163\t                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n164\t        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"}],\n165\t        \"images\": [],\n166\t        \"notes\": \"\",\n167\t    },\n168\t    \"engine_air_filter\": {\n169\t        \"key\": \"engine_air_filter\",\n170\t        \"name\": \"Engine Air Filter\",\n171\t        \"what_it_does\": \"Keeps intake air clean of dust/debris ahead of the MAF/turbo.\",\n172\t        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68248729AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"panel element\",\n173\t                 \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\", \"source\": None}],\n174\t        \"supersedes\": [],\n175\t        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"K&N\", \"number\": \"33-5061\", \"confidence\": \"UNKNOWN\",\n176\t                         \"source\": None}],\n177\t        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T (2017-2022)\",\n178\t        \"location\": \"Airbox, passenger side of the engine bay.\",\n179\t        \"related_codes\": [],\n180\t        \"related_jobs\": [\"engine_air_filter\"],\n181\t        \"torque_keys\": [],\n182\t        \"price\": None,\n183\t        \"buy\": [],\n184\t        \"images\": [],\n185\t        \"notes\": \"\",\n186\t    },\n187\t    \"brake_pads_front\": {\n188\t        \"key\": \"brake_pads_front\",\n189\t        \"name\": \"Front Brake Pad Set\",\n190\t        \"what_it_does\": \"Friction material clamped onto the front rotors by the caliper.\",\n191\t        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68273809AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"front pad set\",\n192\t                 \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\", \"source\": None}],\n193\t        \"supersedes\": [],\n194\t        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Brembo\", \"number\": \"P23165\", \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\",\n195\t                         \"source\": None}],\n196\t        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio, base brakes (2017-2022)\",\n197\t        \"location\": \"Front calipers.\",\n198\t        \"related_codes\": [],\n199\t        \"related_jobs\": [\"brakes_front\"],\n200\t        \"torque_keys\": [\"caliper_slider_front\"],\n201\t        \"price\": {\"low\": 90.0, \"high\": 160.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n202\t                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n203\t        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"}],\n204\t        \"images\": [],\n205\t        \"notes\": \"\",\n206\t    },\n207\t    \"wheel_lug_bolts\": {\n208\t        \"key\": \"wheel_lug_bolts\",\n209\t        \"name\": \"Wheel Lug Bolts\",\n210\t        \"what_it_does\": \"Clamps the wheel to the hub.\",\n211\t        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68247068AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"lug bolt, M14\",\n212\t                 \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\", \"source\": None}],\n213\t        \"supersedes\": [],\n214\t        \"aftermarket\": [],\n215\t        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio (2017-2022)\",\n216\t        \"location\": \"Each wheel, five per corner.\",\n217\t        \"related_codes\": [],\n218\t        \"related_jobs\": [\"wheels\"],\n219\t        \"torque_keys\": [\"wheel_lug\"],\n220\t        \"price\": None,\n221\t        \"buy\": [],\n222\t        \"images\": [],\n223\t        \"notes\": \"\",\n224\t    },\n225\t}\n226\t\n227\t\n228\tdef _fixture_all() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n229\t    return list(_FIXTURE.values())\n230\t\n231\t\n232\tdef _fixture_get(key: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n233\t    return _FIXTURE.get(key)\n234\t\n235\t\n236\tdef _fixture_for_code(code: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n237\t    code = (code or \"\").strip().upper()\n238\t    return [p for p in _FIXTURE.values() if code in (p.get(\"related_codes\") or [])]\n239\t\n240\t\n241\tdef _fixture_for_job(job: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n242\t    job = (job or \"\").strip()\n243\t    return [p for p in _FIXTURE.values() if job in (p.get(\"related_jobs\") or [])]\n244\t\n245\t\n246\t# --- torque resolution -------------------------------------------------------\n247\t\n248\tdef _resolve_torque(key: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n249\t    \"\"\"One ``torque_keys`` entry resolved against the torque libraries.\n250\t\n251\t    Tries ``service_specs`` first, then ``drivetrain_specs`` -- the same\n252\t    order ``cuore.services.service_bridge`` implies by which module it\n253\t    reaches for which job. A key neither recognises still comes back as a\n254\t    row (UNKNOWN), never ``None`` -- a part card should be able to say\n255\t    \"no torque spec found for evap_esim_mount\" rather than silently drop it.\n256\t    \"\"\"\n257\t    for specs in (_service_specs(), _drivetrain_specs()):\n258\t        if specs is None:\n259\t            continue\n260\t        lookup = getattr(specs, \"torque_by_key\", None)\n261\t        if lookup is None:\n262\t            continue\n263\t        try:\n264\t            row = lookup(key)\n265\t        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- a bad key must never 500 a part card\n266\t            row = None\n267\t        if row:\n268\t            return {\n269\t                \"key\": key,\n270\t                \"component\": row.get(\"component\"),\n271\t                \"value\": row.get(\"value\"),\n272\t                \"unit\": row.get(\"unit\"),\n273\t                \"display\": row.get(\"display\"),\n274\t                \"angle\": row.get(\"angle\"),\n275\t                \"single_use\": row.get(\"single_use\"),\n276\t                \"confidence\": row.get(\"confidence\", \"UNKNOWN\"),\n277\t                \"source\": row.get(\"source\"),\n278\t                \"notes\": row.get(\"notes\"),\n279\t            }\n280\t    return {\"key\": key, \"component\": None, \"value\": None, \"unit\": None,\n281\t            \"display\": \"UNKNOWN\", \"angle\": None, \"single_use\": False,\n282\t            \"confidence\": \"UNKNOWN\", \"source\": None,\n283\t            \"notes\": \"no torque spec found for this key -- use the service manual (TechAuthority)\"}\n284\t\n285\t\n286\t_DEFAULTS: dict[str, Any] = {\n287\t    \"name\": \"\", \"what_it_does\": \"\", \"oem\": [], \"supersedes\": [],\n288\t    \"aftermarket\": [], \"fits\": \"\", \"location\": \"\", \"related_codes\": [],\n289\t    \"related_jobs\": [], \"torque_keys\": [], \"price\": None, \"buy\": [],\n290\t    \"images\": [], \"notes\": \"\",\n291\t}\n292\t\n293\t\n294\tdef _enrich(raw: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n295\t    \"\"\"Fill in any field the contract promises but a given row omits, and\n296\t    resolve ``torque_keys`` into a ``torques`` list of full spec rows.\"\"\"\n297\t    out = dict(_DEFAULTS)\n298\t    out.update(raw)\n299\t    out[\"torques\"] = [_resolve_torque(k) for k in (out.get(\"torque_keys\") or [])]\n300\t    return out\n301\t\n302\t\n303\t# --- public API ---------------------------------------------------------\n304\t\n305\tdef part(key: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n306\t    \"\"\"One part by key, enriched with resolved torques -- or ``None`` if no\n307\t    part by that key exists anywhere (real module or fixture).\n308\t\n309\t    ``mes.parts.get()`` returns the record without the key folded in (it's\n310\t    the dict key the caller already has); the fixture's own rows carry\n311\t    ``key`` already. Either way the result below always has it.\n312\t    \"\"\"\n313\t    if not key or not key.strip():\n314\t        return None\n315\t    mod = _parts_mod()\n316\t    try:\n317\t        raw = mod.get(key) if mod is not None else _fixture_get(key)\n318\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n319\t        raw = None\n320\t    if not raw:\n321\t        return None\n322\t    raw = {\"key\": key, **raw}\n323\t    return _enrich(raw)\n324\t\n325\t\n326\tdef _label_siblings(rows: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n327\t    for r in rows:\n328\t        sibling_of = r.get(\"sibling_of\")\n329\t        if sibling_of:\n330\t            r[\"label\"] = f\"from {str(sibling_of).title()} parts: verify fit\"\n331\t    return rows\n332\t\n333\t\n334\tdef parts_for_code(code: str, vin: Optional[str] = None) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n335\t    \"\"\"Every part related to a DTC -- ``[]`` if none are known, never an error.\n336\t\n337\t    ``vin``, if given, resolves a model via ``mes.platform.model_for_vin``\n338\t    and (only against the real ``mes.parts`` module, which supports it --\n339\t    the fixture does not) threads ``include_siblings=True`` through so any\n340\t    sourced sibling-platform part rows are included too, labeled \"from\n341\t    <Model> parts: verify fit\".\n342\t    \"\"\"\n343\t    if not code or not code.strip():\n344\t        return []\n345\t    mod = _parts_mod()\n346\t    include_siblings = bool(_model_for_vin(vin))\n347\t    try:\n348\t        if mod is not None:\n349\t            rows = mod.for_code(code, include_siblings=include_siblings)\n350\t        else:\n351\t            rows = _fixture_for_code(code)\n352\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n353\t        rows = []\n354\t    return _label_siblings([_enrich(r) for r in (rows or [])])\n355\t\n356\t\n357\tdef parts_for_job(job: str, vin: Optional[str] = None) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n358\t    \"\"\"Every part related to a maintenance/service job -- ``[]`` if none.\n359\t    See :func:`parts_for_code` for ``vin``/``include_siblings`` behavior.\"\"\"\n360\t    if not job or not job.strip():\n361\t        return []\n362\t    mod = _parts_mod()\n363\t    include_siblings = bool(_model_for_vin(vin))\n364\t    try:\n365\t        if mod is not None:\n366\t            rows = mod.for_job(job, include_siblings=include_siblings)\n367\t        else:\n368\t            rows = _fixture_for_job(job)\n369\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n370\t        rows = []\n371\t    return _label_siblings([_enrich(r) for r in (rows or [])])\n372\t\n373\t\n374\tdef all_parts() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n375\t    \"\"\"Every part known -- the backing list for the parts page's search box.\n376\t\n377\t    ``mes.parts.all()`` returns ``{key: record}`` (the key not folded into\n378\t    the record, same as ``get()``); the fixture's own ``_fixture_all()``\n379\t    already returns a list of rows each carrying ``key``.\n380\t    \"\"\"\n381\t    mod = _parts_mod()\n382\t    try:\n383\t        if mod is not None:\n384\t            rows = [{\"key\": k, **v} for k, v in mod.all().items()]\n385\t        else:\n386\t            rows = _fixture_all()\n387\t    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n388\t        rows = []\n389\t    return [_enrich(r) for r in (rows or [])]\n390\t\n391\t\n392\tdef search_parts(q: str = \"\") -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n393\t    \"\"\"Case-insensitive substring match over name/key/what-it-does/OEM numbers.\"\"\"\n394\t    rows = all_parts()\n395\t    q = (q or \"\").strip().lower()\n396\t    if not q:\n397\t        return rows\n398\t    out = []\n399\t    for p in rows:\n400\t        haystack = \" \".join([\n401\t            p.get(\"key\", \"\"), p.get(\"name\", \"\"), p.get(\"what_it_does\", \"\"),\n402\t            \" \".join(o.get(\"number\", \"\") or \"\" for o in p.get(\"oem\", [])),\n403\t        ]).lower()\n404\t        if q in haystack:\n405\t            out.append(p)\n406\t    return out\n407\t\n408\t\n409\t__all__ = [\"part\", \"parts_for_code\", \"parts_for_job\", \"all_parts\", \"search_parts\"]\n410\t"}]},"uuid":"31672bb6-9baa-41a2-a6d8-b7318c488177","timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:43:05.684Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\parts_bridge.py","content":"\"\"\"The only module in CUORE that imports :mod:`mes.parts`.\n\n``mes-log-mcp/mes/parts.py`` is being written in parallel by another agent\nand may not exist yet. Every call into it is wrapped and falls back to a\nbuilt-in fixture (shaped exactly like that module's documented contract --\nsee ``_FIXTURE`` below) so the parts page, the ``/api/parts*`` endpoints and\nthe part cards embedded in ``code.html``/``maintenance.html``/\n``oil_change.html``/``brakes_tires.html`` are developable and testable\nbefore it lands. Once ``mes.parts`` exists, nothing here needs to change --\nthe lazy import just starts succeeding and the fixture stops being reached.\n\nContract (``mes.parts``, once it lands): ``get(key)``, ``for_code(code)``,\n``for_job(job)``, ``all()``, each returning / each row shaped::\n\n    {key, name, what_it_does,\n     oem: [{number, brand, note, confidence, source}],\n     supersedes, aftermarket: [{brand, number, confidence, source}],\n     fits, location, related_codes, related_jobs, torque_keys,\n     price: {low, high, currency, as_of, source} | None,\n     buy: [{label, url}],\n     images: [{url, source_page, source_name, kind, licence_note, verified_at}],\n     notes}\n\n``torque_keys`` is a list of keys into the torque libraries -- resolved\nhere, not by ``mes.parts`` itself, against ``mes.service_specs`` and\n``mes.drivetrain_specs`` (the same two libraries\n``cuore.services.service_bridge`` already reaches through its own bridge),\nso a part card can show \"25 Nm, SINGLE-SOURCE\" without ``mes.parts`` needing\nto duplicate the torque library. A key neither library recognises resolves\nto an UNKNOWN row rather than being dropped, so the card can say so.\n\nEvery public function here degrades to an empty result (\"No part data yet\")\nrather than raising -- the one exception is :func:`part`, which returns\n``None`` for an unknown key so the API layer can turn that into a 404.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\n\nfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\n\n\n# --- lazy imports, each independently guarded ------------------------------\n\ndef _parts_mod():\n    \"\"\"``mes.parts``, or ``None`` if it has not landed yet.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        from mes import parts as parts_mod\n        return parts_mod\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- must never be why a page 500s\n        return None\n\n\ndef _service_specs():\n    try:\n        from mes import service_specs\n        return service_specs\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return None\n\n\ndef _drivetrain_specs():\n    try:\n        from mes import drivetrain_specs\n        return drivetrain_specs\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return None\n\n\ndef _model_for_vin(vin: Optional[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"Best-effort model name for ``vin`` via ``mes.platform``, or ``None``\n    on any failure or an unrecognised VIN -- never raises.\"\"\"\n    if not vin:\n        return None\n    try:\n        from mes import platform as platform_mod\n        model = platform_mod.model_for_vin(vin)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return None\n    return None if model == \"UNKNOWN\" else model\n\n\n# --- fixture: the exact shape mes.parts.get()/for_code()/for_job()/all()\n# will return, used until that module lands (or for any key it does not yet\n# cover). Keyed to things this corpus already knows about -- the Stelvio's\n# chronic P0455/P0456 EVAP family (see project_stelvio_evap.md) and the jobs\n# oil_change.html/maintenance.html/brakes_tires.html already render -- so a\n# developer working on those pages sees real-looking cards immediately. ----\n\n_FIXTURE: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {\n    \"esim\": {\n        \"key\": \"esim\",\n        \"name\": \"EVAP Service/Integrity Monitor (ESIM)\",\n        \"what_it_does\": \"Pressurizes the fuel-vapor system and watches the \"\n                        \"decay rate to detect small and large EVAP leaks. A \"\n                        \"failed self-test or a failed component sets \"\n                        \"P0455/P0456/P0457, not necessarily a leak itself.\",\n        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68245527AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\",\n                 \"note\": \"ESIM / natural-vacuum leak-detection pump assembly\",\n                 \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\",\n                 \"source\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/evap-esim-replacement.21004/\"}],\n        \"supersedes\": [],\n        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Standard Motor Products\", \"number\": \"EVAP1234\",\n                         \"confidence\": \"UNKNOWN\", \"source\": None}],\n        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T (2017-2022)\",\n        \"location\": \"Rear of the fuel tank, inline on the vapor line, ahead of the canister.\",\n        \"related_codes\": [\"P0455\", \"P0456\", \"P0457\"],\n        \"related_jobs\": [\"evap_leak\"],\n        \"torque_keys\": [\"evap_esim_mount\"],\n        \"price\": {\"low\": 180.0, \"high\": 260.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"},\n                {\"label\": \"Mopar eStore\", \"url\": \"https://www.moparonlineparts.com\"}],\n        \"images\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/data/esim-photo.jpg\",\n                    \"source_page\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/evap-esim-replacement.21004/\",\n                    \"source_name\": \"stelvioforum.com\", \"kind\": \"product_photo\",\n                    \"licence_note\": \"forum upload, fair-use reference only\",\n                    \"verified_at\": \"2026-09-20\"}],\n        \"notes\": \"Verified against TSB 18-030-17 before replacing -- that TSB's ECM \"\n                 \"calibration read fixes a false P0456 on some build dates without \"\n                 \"any part being replaced.\",\n    },\n    \"purge_valve\": {\n        \"key\": \"purge_valve\",\n        \"name\": \"EVAP Purge Solenoid Valve\",\n        \"what_it_does\": \"Opens under ECM control to let engine vacuum draw stored fuel \"\n                        \"vapor from the canister into the intake. Stuck closed or \"\n                        \"leaking, it can contribute to a P0455/P0456 decay-rate failure.\",\n        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68093419AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\",\n                 \"note\": \"Purge valve/solenoid\", \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\",\n                 \"source\": \"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/purge-valve-location.9821/\"}],\n        \"supersedes\": [\"68093419A (earlier casting, same fit)\"],\n        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Four Seasons\", \"number\": \"PV1029\",\n                         \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\", \"source\": None}],\n        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T (2017-2022)\",\n        \"location\": \"Intake manifold, driver's side, short hose run to the charcoal canister.\",\n        \"related_codes\": [\"P0455\", \"P0456\"],\n        \"related_jobs\": [\"evap_leak\"],\n        \"torque_keys\": [\"evap_purge_valve_mount\"],\n        \"price\": {\"low\": 45.0, \"high\": 90.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"}],\n        \"images\": [],\n        \"notes\": \"\",\n    },\n    \"oil_filter\": {\n        \"key\": \"oil_filter\",\n        \"name\": \"Engine Oil Filter (cartridge element)\",\n        \"what_it_does\": \"Traps combustion byproducts and wear metal out of circulating oil.\",\n        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68105175AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"cartridge element + housing cap\",\n                 \"confidence\": \"CONFIRMED\",\n                 \"source\": \"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/oil-change-maintenance-reset.19336/\"}],\n        \"supersedes\": [],\n        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Mopar/Mann filter element\", \"number\": \"HU 711/51x\",\n                         \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\", \"source\": None}],\n        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T MultiAir (2017-2022)\",\n        \"location\": \"Top of the engine, cartridge-style housing with a plastic cap.\",\n        \"related_codes\": [],\n        \"related_jobs\": [\"oil_change\"],\n        \"torque_keys\": [\"filter_cap\"],\n        \"price\": {\"low\": 18.0, \"high\": 32.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"}],\n        \"images\": [],\n        \"notes\": \"\",\n    },\n    \"engine_air_filter\": {\n        \"key\": \"engine_air_filter\",\n        \"name\": \"Engine Air Filter\",\n        \"what_it_does\": \"Keeps intake air clean of dust/debris ahead of the MAF/turbo.\",\n        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68248729AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"panel element\",\n                 \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\", \"source\": None}],\n        \"supersedes\": [],\n        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"K&N\", \"number\": \"33-5061\", \"confidence\": \"UNKNOWN\",\n                         \"source\": None}],\n        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T (2017-2022)\",\n        \"location\": \"Airbox, passenger side of the engine bay.\",\n        \"related_codes\": [],\n        \"related_jobs\": [\"engine_air_filter\"],\n        \"torque_keys\": [],\n        \"price\": None,\n        \"buy\": [],\n        \"images\": [],\n        \"notes\": \"\",\n    },\n    \"brake_pads_front\": {\n        \"key\": \"brake_pads_front\",\n        \"name\": \"Front Brake Pad Set\",\n        \"what_it_does\": \"Friction material clamped onto the front rotors by the caliper.\",\n        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68273809AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"front pad set\",\n                 \"confidence\": \"SINGLE-SOURCE\", \"source\": None}],\n        \"supersedes\": [],\n        \"aftermarket\": [{\"brand\": \"Brembo\", \"number\": \"P23165\", \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\",\n                         \"source\": None}],\n        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio, base brakes (2017-2022)\",\n        \"location\": \"Front calipers.\",\n        \"related_codes\": [],\n        \"related_jobs\": [\"brakes_front\"],\n        \"torque_keys\": [\"caliper_slider_front\"],\n        \"price\": {\"low\": 90.0, \"high\": 160.0, \"currency\": \"CAD\",\n                  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-20\", \"source\": \"rockauto.com listing\"},\n        \"buy\": [{\"label\": \"RockAuto\", \"url\": \"https://www.rockauto.com\"}],\n        \"images\": [],\n        \"notes\": \"\",\n    },\n    \"wheel_lug_bolts\": {\n        \"key\": \"wheel_lug_bolts\",\n        \"name\": \"Wheel Lug Bolts\",\n        \"what_it_does\": \"Clamps the wheel to the hub.\",\n        \"oem\": [{\"number\": \"68247068AA\", \"brand\": \"Mopar\", \"note\": \"lug bolt, M14\",\n                 \"confidence\": \"CORROBORATED\", \"source\": None}],\n        \"supersedes\": [],\n        \"aftermarket\": [],\n        \"fits\": \"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio (2017-2022)\",\n        \"location\": \"Each wheel, five per corner.\",\n        \"related_codes\": [],\n        \"related_jobs\": [\"wheels\"],\n        \"torque_keys\": [\"wheel_lug\"],\n        \"price\": None,\n        \"buy\": [],\n        \"images\": [],\n        \"notes\": \"\",\n    },\n}\n\n\ndef _fixture_all() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    return list(_FIXTURE.values())\n\n\ndef _fixture_get(key: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n    return _FIXTURE.get(key)\n\n\ndef _fixture_for_code(code: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    code = (code or \"\").strip().upper()\n    return [p for p in _FIXTURE.values() if code in (p.get(\"related_codes\") or [])]\n\n\ndef _fixture_for_job(job: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    job = (job or \"\").strip()\n    return [p for p in _FIXTURE.values() if job in (p.get(\"related_jobs\") or [])]\n\n\n# --- torque resolution -------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _resolve_torque(key: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"One ``torque_keys`` entry resolved against the torque libraries.\n\n    Tries ``service_specs`` first, then ``drivetrain_specs`` -- the same\n    order ``cuore.services.service_bridge`` implies by which module it\n    reaches for which job. A key neither recognises still comes back as a\n    row (UNKNOWN), never ``None`` -- a part card should be able to say\n    \"no torque spec found for evap_esim_mount\" rather than silently drop it.\n    \"\"\"\n    for specs in (_service_specs(), _drivetrain_specs()):\n        if specs is None:\n            continue\n        lookup = getattr(specs, \"torque_by_key\", None)\n        if lookup is None:\n            continue\n        try:\n            row = lookup(key)\n        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- a bad key must never 500 a part card\n            row = None\n        if row:\n            return {\n                \"key\": key,\n                \"component\": row.get(\"component\"),\n                \"value\": row.get(\"value\"),\n                \"unit\": row.get(\"unit\"),\n                \"display\": row.get(\"display\"),\n                \"angle\": row.get(\"angle\"),\n                \"single_use\": row.get(\"single_use\"),\n                \"confidence\": row.get(\"confidence\", \"UNKNOWN\"),\n                \"source\": row.get(\"source\"),\n                \"notes\": row.get(\"notes\"),\n            }\n    return {\"key\": key, \"component\": None, \"value\": None, \"unit\": None,\n            \"display\": \"UNKNOWN\", \"angle\": None, \"single_use\": False,\n            \"confidence\": \"UNKNOWN\", \"source\": None,\n            \"notes\": \"no torque spec found for this key -- use the service manual (TechAuthority)\"}\n\n\n_DEFAULTS: dict[str, Any] = {\n    \"name\": \"\", \"what_it_does\": \"\", \"oem\": [], \"supersedes\": [],\n    \"aftermarket\": [], \"fits\": \"\", \"location\": \"\", \"related_codes\": [],\n    \"related_jobs\": [], \"torque_keys\": [], \"price\": None, \"buy\": [],\n    \"images\": [], \"notes\": \"\",\n}\n\n\ndef _enrich(raw: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Fill in any field the contract promises but a given row omits, and\n    resolve ``torque_keys`` into a ``torques`` list of full spec rows.\"\"\"\n    out = dict(_DEFAULTS)\n    out.update(raw)\n    out[\"torques\"] = [_resolve_torque(k) for k in (out.get(\"torque_keys\") or [])]\n    return out\n\n\n# --- public API ---------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef part(key: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"One part by key, enriched with resolved torques -- or ``None`` if no\n    part by that key exists anywhere (real module or fixture).\n\n    ``mes.parts.get()`` returns the record without the key folded in (it's\n    the dict key the caller already has); the fixture's own rows carry\n    ``key`` already. Either way the result below always has it.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not key or not key.strip():\n        return None\n    mod = _parts_mod()\n    try:\n        raw = mod.get(key) if mod is not None else _fixture_get(key)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        raw = None\n    if not raw:\n        return None\n    raw = {\"key\": key, **raw}\n    return _enrich(raw)\n\n\ndef _label_siblings(rows: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    for r in rows:\n        sibling_of = r.get(\"sibling_of\")\n        if sibling_of:\n            r[\"label\"] = f\"from {str(sibling_of).title()} parts: verify fit\"\n    return rows\n\n\ndef parts_for_code(code: str, vin: Optional[str] = None) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Every part related to a DTC -- ``[]`` if none are known, never an error.\n\n    ``vin``, if given, resolves a model via ``mes.platform.model_for_vin``\n    and (only against the real ``mes.parts`` module, which supports it --\n    the fixture does not) threads ``include_siblings=True`` through so any\n    sourced sibling-platform part rows are included too, labeled \"from\n    <Model> parts: verify fit\".\n    \"\"\"\n    if not code or not code.strip():\n        return []\n    mod = _parts_mod()\n    include_siblings = bool(_model_for_vin(vin))\n    try:\n        if mod is not None:\n            rows = mod.for_code(code, include_siblings=include_siblings)\n        else:\n            rows = _fixture_for_code(code)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        rows = []\n    return _label_siblings([_enrich(r) for r in (rows or [])])\n\n\ndef parts_for_job(job: str, vin: Optional[str] = None) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Every part related to a maintenance/service job -- ``[]`` if none.\n    See :func:`parts_for_code` for ``vin``/``include_siblings`` behavior.\"\"\"\n    if not job or not job.strip():\n        return []\n    mod = _parts_mod()\n    include_siblings = bool(_model_for_vin(vin))\n    try:\n        if mod is not None:\n            rows = mod.for_job(job, include_siblings=include_siblings)\n        else:\n            rows = _fixture_for_job(job)\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        rows = []\n    return _label_siblings([_enrich(r) for r in (rows or [])])\n\n\ndef all_parts() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Every part known -- the backing list for the parts page's search box.\n\n    ``mes.parts.all()`` returns ``{key: record}`` (the key not folded into\n    the record, same as ``get()``); the fixture's own ``_fixture_all()``\n    already returns a list of rows each carrying ``key``.\n    \"\"\"\n    mod = _parts_mod()\n    try:\n        if mod is not None:\n            rows = [{\"key\": k, **v} for k, v in mod.all().items()]\n        else:\n            rows = _fixture_all()\n    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n        rows = []\n    return [_enrich(r) for r in (rows or [])]\n\n\ndef search_parts(q: str = \"\") -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Case-insensitive substring match over name/key/what-it-does/OEM numbers.\"\"\"\n    rows = all_parts()\n    q = (q or \"\").strip().lower()\n    if not q:\n        return rows\n    out = []\n    for p in rows:\n        haystack = \" \".join([\n            p.get(\"key\", \"\"), p.get(\"name\", \"\"), p.get(\"what_it_does\", \"\"),\n            \" \".join(o.get(\"number\", \"\") or \"\" for o in p.get(\"oem\", [])),\n        ]).lower()\n        if q in haystack:\n            out.append(p)\n    return out\n\n\n__all__ = [\"part\", \"parts_for_code\", \"parts_for_job\", \"all_parts\", \"search_parts\"]\n","numLines":410,"startLine":1,"totalLines":410}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fbb765e7-cae8-44e9-8a47-bf86e2ef8508","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"31672bb6-9baa-41a2-a6d8-b7318c488177","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"afed32e1361f5dde3","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfozyYQciauEHDrHPkRTA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WuU5W2xHJR27MM5xfSeyPk","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\api\\parts.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4986,"cache_read_input_tokens":90601,"output_tokens":337,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":191},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4986},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":337,"cache_read_input_tokens":90601,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4986,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4986,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WuU5W2xHJR27MM5xfSeyPk":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\api\\parts.py"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a263e4c0-bd14-4cf0-a61a-d8d7b6397368","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfozyYAjpdStydjoYkY33","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"fbda7b35-c650-42ae-873b-1ac5de3467e7","timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:43:06.046Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"fbda7b35-c650-42ae-873b-1ac5de3467e7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8b9c6287-d7e2-4fd6-8dbd-dc6c5dce5337","agentId":"afed32e1361f5dde3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WuU5W2xHJR27MM5xfSeyPk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"``/api/parts*``: the parts catalog (names, OEM/aftermarket numbers,\n2\tsupersessions, torque specs, price, images), fed by\n3\t:mod:`cuore.services.parts_bridge` -- see that module's docstring for the\n4\tfixture it falls back to while ``mes-log-mcp/mes/parts.py`` is still being\n5\tbuilt in parallel.\n6\t\n7\tEvery page that renders a part card (``/v/{vin}/parts``, and the inline\n8\tcards on ``code.html``/``maintenance.html``/``oil_change.html``/\n9\t``brakes_tires.html``) reaches the same bridge functions this router calls,\n10\tso the page and the JSON cannot disagree.\n11\t\n12\tNot registered on the app here -- ``app.py`` is owned by another agent while\n13\tthis was built. The one line needed there (next to the other ``api``\n14\trouter includes):\n15\t\n16\t    ``app.include_router(parts_api.router, prefix=\"/api\")``\n17\t\n18\t(importing this module as ``from .api import parts as parts_api``.)\n19\t\"\"\"\n20\t\n21\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n22\t\n23\tfrom typing import Any\n24\t\n25\tfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends\n26\t\n27\tfrom ..services import parts_bridge\n28\tfrom ..services.errors import NotFound\n29\tfrom .deps import require_token\n30\t\n31\trouter = APIRouter(tags=[\"parts\"], dependencies=[Depends(require_token)])\n32\t\n33\t\n34\t@router.get(\"/parts\", summary=\"Every part known, with resolved torques\")\n35\tdef list_parts(q: str = \"\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n36\t    rows = parts_bridge.search_parts(q=q) if q else parts_bridge.all_parts()\n37\t    return {\"parts\": rows, \"count\": len(rows)}\n38\t\n39\t\n40\t@router.get(\"/parts/for-code/{code}\", summary=\"Parts related to a DTC\")\n41\tdef parts_for_code(code: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n42\t    rows = parts_bridge.parts_for_code(code)\n43\t    return {\"code\": code.strip().upper(), \"parts\": rows, \"count\": len(rows)}\n44\t\n45\t\n46\t@router.get(\"/parts/for-job/{job}\", summary=\"Parts related to a service/maintenance job\")\n47\tdef parts_for_job(job: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n48\t    rows = parts_bridge.parts_for_job(job)\n49\t    return {\"job\": job, \"parts\": rows, \"count\": len(rows)}\n50\t\n51\t\n52\t@router.get(\"/parts/{key}\", summary=\"One part by key\")\n53\tdef get_part(key: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n54\t    row = parts_bridge.part(key)\n55\t    if row is None:\n56\t        raise NotFound(f\"no part known by key {key!r}\")\n57\t    return row\n58\t\n59\t\n60\t__all__ = [\"router\"]\n61\t"}]},"uuid":"61d40157-e561-44d9-bc25-b11db4fa0364","timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:43:06.069Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\api\\parts.py","content":"\"\"\"``/api/parts*``: the parts catalog (names, OEM/aftermarket numbers,\nsupersessions, torque specs, price, images), fed by\n:mod:`cuore.services.parts_bridge` -- see that module's docstring for the\nfixture it falls back to while ``mes-log-mcp/mes/parts.py`` is still being\nbuilt in parallel.\n\nEvery page that renders a part card (``/v/{vin}/parts``, and the inline\ncards on ``code.html``/``maintenance.html``/``oil_change.html``/\n``brakes_tires.html``) reaches the same bridge functions this router calls,\nso the page and the JSON cannot disagree.\n\nNot registered on the app here -- ``app.py`` is owned by another agent while\nthis was built. The one line needed there (next to the other ``api``\nrouter includes):\n\n    ``app.include_router(parts_api.router, prefix=\"/api\")``\n\n(importing this module as ``from .api import parts as parts_api``.)\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends\n\nfrom ..services import parts_bridge\nfrom ..services.errors import NotFound\nfrom .deps import require_token\n\nrouter = APIRouter(tags=[\"parts\"], dependencies=[Depends(require_token)])\n\n\n@router.get(\"/parts\", summary=\"Every part known, with resolved torques\")\ndef list_parts(q: str = \"\") -> dict[str, Any]:\n    rows = parts_bridge.search_parts(q=q) if q else parts_bridge.all_parts()\n    return {\"parts\": rows, \"count\": len(rows)}\n\n\n@router.get(\"/parts/for-code/{code}\", summary=\"Parts related to a DTC\")\ndef parts_for_code(code: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    rows = parts_bridge.parts_for_code(code)\n    return {\"code\": code.strip().upper(), \"parts\": rows, \"count\": len(rows)}\n\n\n@router.get(\"/parts/for-job/{job}\", summary=\"Parts related to a service/maintenance job\")\ndef parts_for_job(job: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    rows = parts_bridge.parts_for_job(job)\n    return {\"job\": job, \"parts\": rows, \"count\": len(rows)}\n\n\n@router.get(\"/parts/{key}\", summary=\"One part by key\")\ndef get_part(key: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    row = parts_bridge.part(key)\n    if row is None:\n        raise NotFound(f\"no part known by key {key!r}\")\n    return row\n\n\n__all__ = [\"router\"]\n","numLines":61,"startLine":1,"totalLines":61}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fbda7b35-c650-42ae-873b-1ac5de3467e7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
