{"parentUuid":"c3f0a88c-86c5-4a81-b22a-8bd8389361b4","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"afed32e1361f5dde3","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cfp1iDDf6rJgcwjXPxbNc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KEwFurxrNjYnSP8mcfacs4","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Implemented vehicle SYSTEMS as a correlational dimension across the MES toolchain. All 5 requested tests pass (47 + 12 checks).\n\nFiles created:\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\mes\\systems.py — SYSTEMS (16, ordered as specified) with components/live_channels/maintenance_items/parts/depends_on, each depends_on edge sourced (TSB citations from mes.knowledge, mes.parts, mes.code_feel, or SAE J2012 range convention named as generic) or confidence=UNKNOWN with the standard TechAuthority note. `systems_for_code(code, description=\"\")` resolves exact-code table -> any-U-code-is-network -> P1xxx description-keyword match -> SAE range fallback -> honest UNKNOWN; primaries auto-pull their systems' depends_on as role=\"upstream\" rows. `correlate(vin)` builds by_system/co_occurrence/chains/findings from `mes.analysis.dtc_history` (per-session file/timestamp data) plus `mes.workup.build` for active/cleared status, with \"could be upstream\" wording only, never proof.\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\systems_bridge.py — thin pass-through (systems/systems_for_code/correlate), same pattern as known_good_bridge.py/parts_bridge.py.\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\api\\systems.py — GET /systems, /systems/for-code/{code}, /vehicles/{vin}/systems (404 on unknown VIN).\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\tests\\check_systems.py (47 checks) and C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_systems_api.py (12 checks) — both pass.\n\nFiles edited:\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\mes\\__init__.py — added \"systems\" to __all__.\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\server.py — added `from mes import systems as systems_mod` and two new MCP tools: `systems_for_code(code, description=\"\")`, `system_correlation(vin)`.\n\ncuore/app.py was NOT touched (per instructions). Include line to add there, next to the other `api` router includes:\n\n    app.include_router(systems_api.router, prefix=\"/api\")\n\n(with `from .api import systems as systems_api` added to the existing multi-import line in app.py).\n\nVerified against the real Stelvio corpus (VIN ZASFAKPN5J7B88115): evap and network systems both show 12 sessions (>=4 required), with 9 co-occurrence pairs including network/evap (6 of 18 sessions together, lift 0.75). check_server.py and check_workup.py re-run clean — no regressions from the __init__.py/server.py edits.\n\nOne deliberate deviation from the literal task text worth flagging: correlate() calls `mes.analysis.dtc_history(vin=vin)` directly (the same function `mes.workup.build` calls internally) rather than only reading `workup.build(vin)`'s classified history, because that classified view buckets codes into chronic/returned_after_clear/seen_once and silently drops any code with exactly 2 sessions that was never cleared — not enough to compute real per-session co-occurrence. `workup.build` is still used, for current_picture/clear_assessment to classify each system's status (active/cleared_unverified/stale/clean)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_read_input_tokens":172406,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":915,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KEwFurxrNjYnSP8mcfacs4":{"message":"Implemented vehicle SYSTEMS as a correlational dimension across the MES toolchain. All 5 requested tests pass (47 + 12 checks).\n\nFiles created:\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\mes\\systems.py — SYSTEMS (16, ordered as specified) with components/live_channels/maintenance_items/parts/depends_on, each depends_on edge sourced (TSB citations from mes.knowledge, mes.parts, mes.code_feel, or SAE J2012 range convention named as generic) or confidence=UNKNOWN with the standard TechAuthority note. `systems_for_code(code, description=\"\")` resolves exact-code table -> any-U-code-is-network -> P1xxx description-keyword match -> SAE range fallback -> honest UNKNOWN; primaries auto-pull their systems' depends_on as role=\"upstream\" rows. `correlate(vin)` builds by_system/co_occurrence/chains/findings from `mes.analysis.dtc_history` (per-session file/timestamp data) plus `mes.workup.build` for active/cleared status, with \"could be upstream\" wording only, never proof.\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\systems_bridge.py — thin pass-through (systems/systems_for_code/correlate), same pattern as known_good_bridge.py/parts_bridge.py.\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\api\\systems.py — GET /systems, /systems/for-code/{code}, /vehicles/{vin}/systems (404 on unknown VIN).\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\tests\\check_systems.py (47 checks) and C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_systems_api.py (12 checks) — both pass.\n\nFiles edited:\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\mes\\__init__.py — added \"systems\" to __all__.\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\server.py — added `from mes import systems as systems_mod` and two new MCP tools: `systems_for_code(code, description=\"\")`, `system_correlation(vin)`.\n\ncuore/app.py was NOT touched (per instructions). Include line to add there, next to the other `api` router includes:\n\n    app.include_router(systems_api.router, prefix=\"/api\")\n\n(with `from .api import systems as systems_api` added to the existing multi-import line in app.py).\n\nVerified against the real Stelvio corpus (VIN ZASFAKPN5J7B88115): evap and network systems both show 12 sessions (>=4 required), with 9 co-occurrence pairs including network/evap (6 of 18 sessions together, lift 0.75). check_server.py and check_workup.py re-run clean — no regressions from the __init__.py/server.py edits.\n\nOne deliberate deviation from the literal task text worth flagging: correlate() calls `mes.analysis.dtc_history(vin=vin)` directly (the same function `mes.workup.build` calls internally) rather than only reading `workup.build(vin)`'s classified history, because that classified view buckets codes into chronic/returned_after_clear/seen_once and silently drops any code with exactly 2 sessions that was never cleared — not enough to compute real per-session co-occurrence. `workup.build` is still used, for current_picture/clear_assessment to classify each system's status (active/cleared_unverified/stale/clean)."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c35c4594-6695-4e73-8860-7515d1a48624","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfp1iCyX9BZWdjpYHEp54","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"24bc6dc8-482e-4146-a9cd-f9c7c4a3f29a","timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:52:55.208Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
